/-
# Theorem V_i: the margin inequality (PROOF_TI2 §0, §6)

`margin_Vi_proof`: `alphaT n + betaT n < 0` whenever `marginOK n` (Lean's constant `Φ_L = −1.3538792` in `betaT`, not the
paper's `Φ_U`). Model: `Chi2U/VOdd/Margin.lean` (whose `logN_le`/`logN_ge`, `log_sqrt5_le`, `Gs`, `log_odd`, `term_le`,
`sum_hcor_le` are reused) and `Chi2U/V/Margin.lean` (`log_nat_eq`, `cSV_eq`, `sum_g_le`, `log_zU_four`).

Route:
* `z = zT n` satisfies `z² − n z + 1 = 0` and `z ≤ 1/(n − 1)`, so `log(n z) = log(1 + z²) ≤ z² ≤ 1/(n − 1)²`, i.e.
  `−log z_n ≥ log n − 1/(n − 1)²` (`log_zT_le`; sharper than the paper's `u_n ≥ n − 1`, which the thin cases
  `n = 115, 71` cannot afford);
* with `log n = ν log 2 + Σ v_p log p` and `cSV n = ¼ Σ v_p log p + G(n)`, `G(n) = Σ_{p ∣ n odd} log p/(4(p − 1))`:
  `M(n) ≤ K + c₂ − ν log 2/4 + G(n) − ¼ log n + 1/(2(n − 1)²)`, `K = 4/3 + Φ_L + ½ log(√5 + 2) ≈ 0.701272`
  (`margin_le`);
* `n ≡ 0 mod 4` (`ν ≥ 2`, `n ≥ 8`; `margin_nu2`): `G ≤ ⅛ Σ v_p log p` gives `M ≤ K − (9/8) log 2 + 1/98 < −0.068`;
* `n ≡ 2 mod 4`, `n ≥ 138` (`margin_nu1_large`): `M ≤ K − ⅛ log 2 − ⅛ log 138 + 1/(2·137²) < −0.0012`;
* odd `n ≥ 275` (`margin_odd_large`): V_odd's split of `p = 3, 5, 7`,
  `M ≤ K + ½ log 2 + log 3/10 + 3 log 5/80 + log 7/60 − (9/40) log 275 + 1/(2·274²) < −0.013`;
* the 113 remaining values (`finL`: `n ≡ 2 mod 4` with `22 ≤ n < 138`, `n ≠ 30`; odd `71 ≤ n < 275`, `n ∉ EOddI`) case
  by case (`M_n`), `log` enclosed by `logPt 30` (`decide +kernel`), `log 2` by Mathlib's 9-digit bounds. Generated by
  `scripts/ti/margin_ti_cases.py --gen` (output `scripts/ti/margin_ti_cases.out`), which also recomputes every margin
  in Arb (200 bits): for `5 ≤ n ≤ 20000` the set `{M(n) ≥ 0}` is exactly the complement of `marginOK`. Thinnest margins:
  `n = 115` (`−0.00213`), `71` (`−0.00250`), `129` (`−0.00736`), `73` (`−0.00978`).
Departure from PROOF_TI2 §6: the tails are the three closed forms above (thresholds 8, 138, 275) instead of the uniform
`P = 13` tail (which with `Φ_L` is negative only from `n = 613`), and the finite range is checked in Lean instead of the
Arb table.
-/
